## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a privacy-preserving, multi-tenant AI workflow at scale, with strict data isolation, governance, and measurable latency.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant OpenAI deployment and prompt routing
- Real-time ingestion (Event Hubs) and low-latency scoring
- KB grounding via Cognitive Search on Blob data
- PII redaction (Text Analytics) and per-tenant masking (Key Vault)
- RBAC (Azure AD), Data Lake auditing, canary rollout

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: route prompt for tenant, redact, ground, respond
async function handleRequest(req){
  const tenantId = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  const raw = req.body;
  const redacted = redactPII(raw);
  const kb = loadKBVersion(tenantId);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(redacted, kb, tenantId);
  const resp = await openai.complete(prompt, {deployment: getDeployment(tenantId)});
  logAudit(tenantId, prompt, resp);
  return resp;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to quantify latency vs. isolation trade-offs?
- How to implement drift detection for the KB and prompts across tenants?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical security-first design for Azure OpenAI with code-gen, focusing on secret redaction, key vault integration, tenant isolation, and auditable logging.

## Key Concepts
- Secret management with Azure Key Vault and Managed Identity
- Request/response redaction and policy enforcement
- Data isolation per tenant and private networking
- End-to-end auditing in Purview
- Testing: redaction fuzzing and integration tests

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: redact secrets before sending to OpenAI
function redact(input, keys){
  let out = input;
  keys.forEach(k => { out = out.replace(new RegExp(k, 'g'), 'REDACTED'); });
  return out;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test drift in redaction rules across tenants?
- What data plane logs would you guard and what retention policy would you apply?

## Why This Is Asked
This probes practical Azure OpenAI integration with APIM, Functions, Redis, and Table Storage, focusing on latency, data governance, and beginner-friendly design.

## Key Concepts
- API Management gating
- Data redaction
- Redis caching for performance
- Azure Table Storage FAQ catalog
- Latency testing and basic observability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Redaction function
function redactPII(text) {
  return text
    .replace(/\b[A-Z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Z0-9.-]+\.[A-Z]{2,}\b/gi, "[REDACTED_EMAIL]")
    .replace(/\b\d{3}-\d{2}-\d{4}\b/g, "[REDACTED_SSN]");
}
```

```javascript
// Redis cache lookup
async function getAnswer(query) {
  const key = `faq:${query}`;
  let cached = await redis.get(key);
  if (cached) return JSON.parse(cached);
  const answer = await fetchFromTable(query);
  await redis.set(key, JSON.stringify(answer), { EX: 300 });
  return answer;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test cache eviction and cold-start behavior?
- How would you handle multilingual queries in this flow?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design a comprehensive Azure OpenAI solution that integrates multiple Azure services while addressing key enterprise requirements like multilingual support, data governance, and cost management in a beginner-friendly scenario.

## Key Concepts
- Language detection and per-tenant language preference management
- Per-language knowledge bases stored in Azure Blob Storage
- Real-time translation layer and content grounding via Azure Cognitive Search
- PII redaction and per-tenant budget enforcement mechanisms
- API Management routing policies and comprehensive auditing to Azure Data Lake

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: detect language, translate, search knowledge base, query OpenAI, translate back
const lang = detectLanguage(request);
const kb = await loadLanguageKB(lang);
const translatedQuery = await translateToEnglish(request, lang);
const groundedContext = await cognitiveSearch(translatedQuery, kb);
const response = await callOpenAI(groundedContext);
return translateFromEnglish(response, lang);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement currency and locale handling while ensuring no PII leakage across language translations?
- How would you scale this architecture to handle multiple tenants with different language support requirements?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end RAG pipelines with governance in a realistic Azure stack.

## Key Concepts
- Retrieval augmented generation, vector search, API Management, per-tenant residency, secret redaction, monitoring.
- Access controls, cost vs latency trade-offs, data provenance.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Redact secrets from user prompt
function redactPrompt(input){
  return input.replace(/(password|token|secret)\s*=\s*\S+/gi, '$1=REDACTED');
}
```

```javascript
// Simple guardrail stub: block disallowed topics in response
function guardResponse(text){
  const forbidden=[/internal-credential|secret-key/i];
  for(const f of forbidden){
    if(f.test(text)) return text.replace(f, 'REDACTED');
  }
  return text;
}
```

